.TH CFOREGDUMP 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
CFORegDump \- print a formatted dump of a CFO's registers and counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B CFORegDump
.RB [ \-d
.IR cfo ]
.RB [ \-R ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Constructs
.B CFOLib::CFO_Registers
with
.B skipInit
set and prints the formatted register dump
.RB ( formattedDumpFunctions_ )
and, with
.BR \-s ,
the counters
.RB ( formattedCounterFunctions_ ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " cfo"
Card index.
Default:
.B CFOLIB_CFO
if set, else
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
else 0.
.TP
.B \-R
Do not print the register dump.
.TP
.B \-s
Print the counter registers.
.TP
.B \-h
Usage, exit 0.
The usage also lists
.BR \-p ;
it is not implemented and is reported as an unknown option.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; abort (134) if the device cannot be opened.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR CFOLIB_CFO ,
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ;
.B CFOLIB_SIM_ENABLE
(then
.BR DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE )
overrides the hardware mode as in
.BR DTCRegDump (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
CFORegDump \-d 0 \-s
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR DTCRegDump (1),
.BR cfoUtil (1),
.BR libCFOInterface (3),
.BR mu2e (4)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
Manual page written for the September 2026 DAQ mega-review from the source
at commit a5c0ce7.
